      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is an old issue that was around with the original Rift. It would happen when the game would detect slight upward movement from your thumbstick even without you pushing it. The only way to fix the thumbstick drift is to blow air into it. Though it is also possible your problem is a glitch in the game, but most people I've met found out it was because of thumbstick drift.",
